  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Interaction with the Resource Index.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "The idea is to search a GSearch index by embedding a Lucene query in an iTQL query , ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "and the opposite, to search the Resource Index by embedding an iTQL query in a Lucene query. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Example of iTQL query with embedded Lucene query:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "select $object1 $object2 from <#ri>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "where $object1 <fedora-model:hasModel> <info:fedora/MyNS:XContentModel>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "and $object1 <fgsearch-MyIndex:matches> 'author:Jones AND fulltext:(salt AND water)'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "and $object2 <fedora-model:hasModel> <info:fedora/MyNS:YContentModel>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "and $object1 <my-model:hasRelationTo> $object2",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "This overcomes the two weaknesses that Lucene cannot do joins, ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "and that the full-text option of the Resource Index uses Lucene in a limited manner ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "(e.g. you cannot search on the full document text behind a pdf datastream, ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "and you cannot exploit numerous features of Lucene and Solr).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
