  "description": "<p>Interaction with the Resource Index.<br/>\nThe idea is to search a GSearch index by embedding a Lucene query in an iTQL query , <br/>\nand the opposite, to search the Resource Index by embedding an iTQL query in a Lucene query. <br/>\nExample of iTQL query with embedded Lucene query:<br/>\nselect $object1 $object2 from &lt;#ri&gt;<br/>\nwhere $object1 &lt;fedora-model:hasModel&gt; &lt;info:fedora/MyNS:XContentModel&gt;<br/>\nand $object1 &lt;fgsearch-MyIndex:matches&gt; 'author:Jones AND fulltext:(salt AND water)'<br/>\nand $object2 &lt;fedora-model:hasModel&gt; &lt;info:fedora/MyNS:YContentModel&gt;<br/>\nand $object1 &lt;my-model:hasRelationTo&gt; $object2<br/>\nThis overcomes the two weaknesses that Lucene cannot do joins, <br/>\nand that the full-text option of the Resource Index uses Lucene in a limited manner <br/>\n(e.g. you cannot search on the full document text behind a pdf datastream, <br/>\nand you cannot exploit numerous features of Lucene and Solr).</p>",
